From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:47:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/57] panfrost: Add cull distance emulation passes

Mali has no native cull distance. Emulate it with the fragment discard
path already used for clip. The vertex shader emits, per cull distance, a
linear quantity (cull distance >= 0) into VARYING_SLOT_CULL_PRIMITIVE.
The fragment prolog demotes a fragment where that quantity is identically
zero across the primitive, detected as a zero value with zero
screen-space derivatives. That is exactly the condition that every vertex
of the primitive has a negative cull distance, so the whole primitive is
culled without clipping straddle primitives.

The real cull distances stay in CLIP_DIST0/1 for gl_CullDistance reads.
One demote and one ATEST cover both clip and cull.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c |   6 +-
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.h        |   4 +
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_nir_prolog.c      | 141 +++++++++++++++++---
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_nir_prolog.h      |  10 +-
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c       |   2 +-
 5 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

